ce category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1104008A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources> </nplcit> </non-patent-citations> </citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KITAGAWA KOUICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MATSUSHITA ELECTRONICS CORP</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MYOJO MINORU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>UEDA TAKASHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KITAGAWA, KOUICHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUSHITA ELECTRONICS CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MYOJO, MINORU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>UEDA, TAKASHI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KITAGAWA KOUICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MYOJO MINORU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>UEDA TAKASHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KITAGAWA, KOUICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MYOJO, MINORU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>UEDA, TAKASHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A fluorescent lamp (10) comprises a bulb (2), on each end of which is provided an electrode coil (3) suspended between two leads (4a, 4b) supported on an end glass (5). Overheat protection means (20) of the end glass is suspended between the leads (4a, 4b) located between the electrode coil (3) and the end glass (5). The overheat protection means (20) consists of a glass material (21) and first and second metal pins (22a, 22b) for supporting the glass material (20). The metal pins (22a, 22b), not in contact with each other, are connected with the corresponding leads (4a, 4b) on one end. The glass material (20) is heated by conduction, radiation and pulsating discharge toward the end of service life when the emitter has been almost consumed but the coil is still conducting, and the glass material (20) finally melts by ion conduction when the electrode coil (3) becomes broken. As a result, the end glass remains unmelted, thus keeping the fluorescent lamp undestroyed.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Cette lampe à fluorescence (10) comprend une ampoule (2) dont chaque extrémité possède un bobinage d'électrode (3) suspendu entre deux fils (4a, 4b) montés sur un verre d'extrémité (5). Un dispositif de protection contre la surchauffe (20) du verre d'extrémité est suspendu entre les fils (4a, 4b) se trouvant entre le bobinage d'électrode (3) et le verre d'extrémité (5). Ce dispositif de protection contre la surchauffe (20) est en verre (21) et comporte deux broches métalliques (22a, 22b) soutenant la partie en verre (20). Les broches métalliques (22a, 22b), qui n'entrent pas en contact, sont reliées aux fils correspondants (4a, 4b) sur une extrémité. Le verre (20) est chauffé par conduction, rayonnement et décharge pulsatile vers la fin de la durée de vie lorsque l'émetteur a été presque consommé mais que le bobinage est toujours conducteur. Le verre (20) fond finalement sous l'effet de la conduction ionique lorsque le bobinage d'électrode (3) est rompu. Il en résulte que le verre d'extrémité ne fond pas, ce qui évite la destruction de la lampe.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>